WHEN WE CONNECT, MEANINGFUL THINGS HAPPENWe've created a place designed around the power of meaningful connections. Everything is right here, under our roof and within easy reach. A place for dynamic interactions.

‘Are you looking for an internship with the perfect balance between operations and administration?'

YES, because you want&hellip;

• to be a buzzing central centipede;

• to be an important piece of the big puzzle;

• to work together with the Purchasing Manager;

• to be the point of contact for employees and suppliers;

• to roll up your sleeves and be responsibility of the daily operations in the purchasing department;

• to take on challenges and tackles this in a team effort;

• to know all the ins and outs regarding Purchasing and finance administration, including to be knowledge about all the systems, stock control and accounts payable.

WE offer:

• a great place to work with a canal view;

• an entry into the World of Hyatt, where internships may lead into jobs;

• international working experience;

• great intern working conditions (read: EUR 650/month intern allowance, loads of training opportunities, potential career planning, discounts all over the world and let's not forget about our social activities&hellip;!)

Functie-eisen:
You are&hellip;

• currently enrolled in a hospitality or tourism-related study program;

• trustworthy;

• always seeking for opportunities and creative solutions that enhance efficiency and effectiveness;

• hands-on, pro-active and enthusiastic;

• available for five months or longer from the start date mentioned in the vacancy title;

• not afraid to make decisions;

• detail-oriented and approachable;

• very communicative in English (and preferably in Dutch);

•  holding an EU/EEA passport OR enrolled in a Dutch School.

If the above is what you want and who you are, please upload your CV and tell us all about you!

CANDIDATES ARE EXPECTED TO ADD THEIR DESIRED START DATE, INTERNSHIP DURATION AND CONFIRM T

- Venlo - 40 uur - € 15,68 per uur 
Are you someone who likes to roll up their sleeves, works accurately and enjoys a dynamic working environment? Then we are looking for you! As a Warehouse Employee, you will work in a modern distribution centre in Venlo, where you and your colleagues are responsible for processing and preparing orders for shipment across Europe and the Middle East. 
What do we offer? 
• A gross hourly wage of €15.68; 
• A full-time position of 40 hours per week; 
• A high chance of receiving a permanent contract; 
• Double pay on Sundays and public holidays; 
• Travel allowance of €0.21 per kilometre; 
• Flexible day shifts between 07:00 and 19:00; 
• 30% overtime allowance; 
• 200% pay on Sundays; 
• Paid training and plenty of opportunities for personal and professional development; 
• Working in a modern and sustainable distribution centre in Venlo; 
• An international and dynamic working environment; 
• Access to an exclusive Sample Sale featuring well-known fashion brands. 
What will you do? 
As a Warehouse Employee, you are an important part of the logistics process. 
Your responsibilities will include: - Picking and processing orders for customers across Europe and the Middle East; - Picking fashion items in the warehouse; - Moving and processing goods within the warehouse; - Checking orders and preparing them for shipment; - Identifying and reporting discrepancies and quality issues; - Working together with colleagues and supervisors to ensure orders are processed correctly and on time; - Keeping the workplace clean and safe; - Working according to applicable safety and quality regulations. 
What do you bring? - You are willing to work weekends; - You speak and understand English, as this is the main language spoken on the work floor; - You are motivated, reliable and hardworking; - You work accurately and have an eye for quality; - Experience in logistics is a plus, but motivation and a good work ethic are...

This is not your average production environment. The organisation you'll be joining is a global frontrunner in identity security, think biometric passports, secure payment cards, facial recognition at international airports, and cryptographic systems used by governments and banks worldwide. 

As Maintenance Engineer, you are the backbone of a smooth-running production floor. When machines go down, you're the one who gets things moving again, but more importantly, you make sure they don't go down in the first place. You combine hands-on technical skill with a structured mindset: you don't just fix problems, you prevent them. 

What you'll be doing

- Keeping production equipment in top condition and reducing unplanned downtime;
- Building and executing preventive maintenance schedules;
- Digging into the root cause of breakdowns — not just patching things up;
- Translating technical findings into clear documentation and practical improvement plans;
- Supporting the roll-out and commissioning of new equipment;
- Working with software controls for production machinery;
- Collaborating with production, management, and other departments on both day-to-day operations and longer-term reliability improvements;
- Monitoring facility and utility systems to ensure a safe working environment.

- An MBO level 4 background in Electrical or Manufacturing Engineering (or equivalent experience);
- A proven track record in a maintenance role within a production environment;
- Good command of English, spoken and written;
- Flexibility to work in shifts and join an on-call rotation;
- Willingness to occasionally travel for training or visits to other sites;
- Strong communication skills and a collaborative attitude.
